#CONFLICT  IN GIT WHILE PULLING FROM PRODUCTION /GITHUB VERSION TO DEVELOPMENT

1-check what conflicted RUN: git status
2-check the differeces in conflict files in production/Developme e.g RUN: git diff -- frontend/tailwind.config.js
3-choose the production/GitHub version with: git checkout --theirs frontend/tailwind.config.js 
  or choose :git checkout --ours frontend/tailwind.config.js
  Don't stage it yet.
  Then display the entire local version:type frontend\tailwind.config.js
  Then we'll compare it against the production version using:
    - #production:
      git show origin/main:frontend/tailwind.config.js
    - #development:
      git show HEAD:frontend/src/pages/Home.tsx
      
4-Then mark the conflict as resolved: git add frontend/tailwind.config.js